    "title": "OBITUARY: Linzy Wilson \"Tim\" Blair - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Carpenter ,\n9 hours ago Linzy “Tim” Wilson Blair was born on January 23, 1940, in Lawshe, Ohio, to the late Tom Blair and Thelma Michael Blair. He passed away on September 29, 2026, at NHC Healthcare in Franklin, Tennessee.\nAlong with his parents, Tim was preceded in death by his siblings, Dewey, Virginia, Edith, Rosie, Mary “Ruth,” Lilly, George, Clara, Betty, Fred, and Berlin.\nHe is lovingly survived by his wife Freda Merideth Blair; daughter, Kim (Matt) Hawkins; sons, Tim (Rebecca) Blair and Nicholas Blair; five grandchildren Sydney, Maverik, Haley, Will, and Brian; and sisters, Carol and Sharon.\nTim proudly served his country in the United States Army. Throughout his working years, he made his living as a truck driver and was known for his strong work ethic and willingness to work hard to provide for those he loved.\nA gentle soul at heart, Tim found happiness in the simple things in life. He had a special love for horses and enjoyed spending time on the farm. He was a hardworking man with a quiet and gentle nature, and the life he lived reflected his devotion to his family and the things that mattered most to him.\nFor more obituaries visit our obituaries page .\nThis obituary was published by McDonald Funeral Home, Inc. – Hickman County .",
    "summary": "Along with his parents, Tim was preceded in death by his siblings, Dewey, Virginia, Edith, Rosie, Mary “Ruth,” Lilly, George, Clara, Betty, Fred, and Berlin. A gentle soul at heart, Tim found happiness in the simple things in life. He had a special love for horses and enjoyed spending time on the farm. He was a hardworking man with a quiet and gentle nature, and the life he lived reflected his devotion to his family and the things that mattered most to him. This obituary was published by McDonald Funeral Home, Inc. – Hickman County .",
